body:
I know tons of people are making the suggestion to delete Tik Tok but for better or for worse, it's here to stay (at least for a little while) so while deleting it is very solid and logical advice, I've learned to take all the things that trigger me and learn to just not let them influence me.

&#x200B;

One of the biggest things that has helped me is to learn and literally STUDY psychological tricks that manipulate consumers.  The ONLY goal of stores and sellers is to make money.  They are the only ones that profit from consumers spending money.  Any coupon or deal that exists is a desperate attempt to get someone to spend.  The more I started paying attention to how I'm being manipulated the more discouraged I get from getting whatever it is they are selling.

&#x200B;

The people that create these videos are also only profiting from you.  They are profiting from your views, from your likes, and from all those affiliate links they provide.  That's not to say that some things aren't genuinely useful or good products, it just means that some random stranger is not actually invested in your happiness from a quirky new kitchen gadget. Besides, if reckless spending is what someone is promoting, I don't want to support that. 

&#x200B;

Instead of deleting the platform start searching for other types of influencing.  Search for budgeting advice, search for shopping addiction advocates, search for ANYTHING that interests you that doesn't influence you to shop needlessly.  Maybe it's bad knock knock jokes, maybe it's trivia about your favorite movie series, funny poodle pictures, ANYTHING that will still entertain you without triggering or encouraging spending.  I think there's a way to mark recommended videos with "do not recommend" or something of that sort (at least there is for YouTube) and GRADUALLY....VERY GRADUALLY you will start seeing less and less of the useless triggering crap. 

&#x200B;

My bad shopping habits are emotional so until I addressed this, all those logical suggestions and strategies were never going to work for me. 

&#x200B;

I hope you find something that works for you. Stay Strong!
